## Story Description
Add two endpoints to backend/app/routers/recommendations.py. GET /config returns the current per-engagement recommendation thresholds as a flat dict (config.yaml defaults merged with any recommendation_config_json overrides stored on the engagement row). PATCH /config accepts a partial RecommendationConfigUpdate Pydantic body, merges the non-None fields into the existing stored JSON, and persists to engagements.recommendation_config_json. Both endpoints call verify_engagement_ownership and load_config() using the SPENDCUBE_CONFIG_PATH env var.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Edit file: backend/app/routers/recommendations.py — add import os at the top if not present; add 'from src.config import load_config' import inside the endpoint functions (following existing lazy-import pattern in this file)
- Edit file: backend/app/routers/recommendations.py — add Pydantic model RecommendationConfigUpdate(BaseModel) with all Optional fields: consolidation_threshold: Optional[int] = None; target_payment_days: Optional[int] = None; wacc: Optional[float] = None; min_wc_opportunity: Optional[int] = None; tail_spend_alert_pct: Optional[float] = None; maverick_alert_pct: Optional[float] = None; competitive_tender_min_spend: Optional[float] = None; contract_coverage_gap_min_spend: Optional[float] = None; concentration_threshold_pct: Optional[float] = None; min_discount_opportunity: Optional[float] = None
- Edit file: backend/app/routers/recommendations.py — add GET /config endpoint decorated with @router.get('/config'): verify_engagement_ownership; load config defaults; query SELECT recommendation_config_json FROM engagements WHERE id = :eid; build defaults_dict from config.recommendations model_dump(); if stored JSON exists, merge into defaults_dict; return merged dict
- Edit file: backend/app/routers/recommendations.py — add PATCH /config endpoint decorated with @router.patch('/config'): verify_engagement_ownership; query existing recommendation_config_json; parse existing JSON or start with {}; update with body.model_dump(exclude_none=True); persist json.dumps(merged) back to engagements.recommendation_config_json; return merged dict
- Run: cd backend && python -c "from app.routers.recommendations import router; paths = [r.path for r in router.routes]; print(paths)" — output list must contain strings ending in '/config'

